/*  EXPECTED: COMPILES and runs; compiled output must match the interpreter.

    An object made in a rabbit with a field made there; a rabbit's series is inserted through the field.

    Nothing here outlives its region, and nothing is refused: every store is judged against
    where its target really lives (docs/SOUNDNESS.md, obligation O2). */

Define object bag with (the series of series of number items).
Pull a rabbit.
    Define b as a new bag { the items (a series of series of number) }.
    Define inner as a series of number with (1, 2, 3).
    Insert inner into b's items.
    State the number of b's items.
Done.
